            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "kEsZx",
              "name": "Idea",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 6,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "MEj2Z",
                  "name": "Label",
                  "fill": "$subtle",
                  "content": "Idea",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "500"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "l1m2Jy",
                  "name": "Body",
                  "fill": "$prose",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The site already speaks in dither. This bakes it in: each thumb is a dense crop of the real product, ordered-dithered into that brand's ink and paper (Sway blue, Cerebro violet, BenKon sky, GreenMaster green). The only full-colour pixel group is the app icon, so the icon is what you recognise and the texture is what tells them apart.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "NgNsV",
              "name": "Production",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 6,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "vBQj2",
                  "name": "Label",
                  "fill": "$subtle",
                  "content": "Production",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "500"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Q7FoI",
                  "name": "Body",
                  "fill": "$prose",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The dither is the repo's image-dither.glsl as a Pencil shader effect on the screen layer (2 px cell, 3 levels, per-brand ink and paper), so Export bakes it into the PNG. Then cwebp to 512x320. On the site, set the row's reveal to a plain fade or skip the extra shader, since the thumb is already dithered.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "k0yHC",
              "name": "Pros and cons",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 6,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "wpR3O",
                  "name": "Label",
                  "fill": "$subtle",
                  "content": "Pros and cons",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "500"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hLgvY",
                  "name": "Body",
                  "fill": "$prose",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "+ Privacy by construction: even the 2x webp can't be read, so any screenshot is usable. + Most on-brand for this site, and the four still differ by hue. - Hover reveal has less to reveal (dither to brighter dither). - Duotone at 128x80 can turn to noise if the crop is too busy; crops must have big shapes.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
